==Maori==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*tili}} (“hand net” – compare with {{cognate|sm|tili}} “to cast a net, to [[net]]”, {{cognate|haw|kili}} “to [[rain]] gently, to [[drizzle]]”, {{cognate|ty|tiri}}, {{cognate|to|sili}} “to net”)<ref name="T">{{cite-book|title=Maori-Polynesian Comparative Dictionary|first= Edward|last=Tregear|year=1891|publisher=Lyon and Blair |location=Wellington, New Zealand|page=517|url=https://nzetc.victoria.ac.nz/tm/scholarly/tei-TreMaor-c1-12.html}}</ref><ref>{{R:Pollex|tili.1a}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal | last =Osmond  | first = Meredith |authorlink=Meredith Osmond |title=Proto Oceanic terms for fishing and hunting implements | journal= Oceanic Studies: Proceedings of the First International Conference on Oceanic Linguistics|volume=C-133 |page=115|publisher= The Australian National University|year= 1996 }}</ref>

===Verb===
{{mi-verb|a}}

# to [[cast]], to [[scatter]]
#: {{syn|mi|rū|rui|whakamarara|whakaehu}}
# to throw or place one by one, to [[stack]] in a [[row]]
#: {{syn|mi|whakarārangi}}
# to [[plant]]
#: {{syn|mi|tanu}}
# to [[share]]
#: {{syn|mi|wāhi}}

